That explains why most folks on the newsgroup think
daggers are so important.  You don't waste a turn
each wielding and unwielding.

But consider - The DevTeam coded monster behavior to
wield different weapons at different ranges.  They
think it's worth that extra turn.  As soon as a monster
gets in arrow range it will wield its bow and start
shooting.  As soon as it gets within dagger range it
will throw a dagger or knife without wielding it.
And as soon as it comes face to face it spends that
turn to switch.  Fire constantly with every resource
and only stop firing to change when the next type of
resource can be used, that's the strategy the DevTeam
gave monsters.  The wasted turn, that's why characters
collect stacks of daggers.

Rangers get the Longbow of Diana in the Quest IIRC.
To me that's the only class I'd want to wield a bow
once I amassed a big stack of daggers.



